# GUI button click tooltips

HexaCore `Button.setFunctionality(callback, description, clickTypes)` registers the handler **and** appends a how-to-use line via `Icon.addHowToUse`, e.g. `<Click to choose your path>`.

Do **not** add manual lore that repeats the same instruction.

## Use `setFunctionality` for the click hint

```java
// ❌ BAD — duplicate click instructions in lore and tooltip
icon.addLore("");
icon.addLore(String.format("%sClick to choose founder or friends.", CivColor.Gold));
objectiveButton.setFunctionality(click -> openChoiceHandler.run(), "choose your path", ClickType.LEFT, ClickType.RIGHT);

// ✅ GOOD — description is the action phrase; tooltip is generated once
objectiveButton.setFunctionality(click -> openChoiceHandler.run(), "choose your path", ClickType.LEFT, ClickType.RIGHT);
```

Pass a short **verb phrase** as `description` (what the click does), not a full sentence with "Click to…". The framework prefixes it with the click type.

## What still belongs in lore

- Title, gray description, progress, status (completed / locked / optional)
- Requirements, costs, errors — anything that is **not** the click action
- Blank line between sections (see `java-civcolor-formatting`)

## Non-clickable buttons

If the button has **no** `setFunctionality`, there is no auto tooltip — use lore for any guidance the player needs.

## Multiple click bindings

Each `setFunctionality` call adds another how-to-use line for its `ClickType`s (e.g. left vs right). Do not mirror those in `addLore` either.
